# Normalise text to LF in the working tree, not just in the index.
#
# Several contract tests pin a SHA-256 digest over file content
# (scripts/test-m5-00*-schema-contract.ts) or regex production source. Those
# digests were computed over LF. With core.autocrlf=true and no rules here, a
# Windows checkout materialises CRLF and the digests can never match, so the
# contracts fail locally while passing in Linux CI — a false failure that
# hides real ones.
#
# After changing this file, existing working copies must be renormalised once:
#   git add --renormalize .
# Review and commit that on its own; it touches every text file.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
